  "premise": "Directional event information is conditional on location relative to a confirmed major level: the same event at a confirmed major level has positive forward edge, while away from structure it does not.",
  "economic_rationale": "Confirmed major pivots concentrate resting liquidity, stop orders, and market-maker inventory. A directional event at a level is a liquidity interaction with a counterparty flow; the same event mid-range has no such mechanism. M2 averaged locations in an unconditional vote, M3 conditioned on state but still averaged locations, and the 15m family programme tested the families unconditionally.",
